      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with clear morning skies giving way to a mixed bag of weather, light snow flurries and sunny spells before cloud increases in the afternoon. There's been 7 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently -2°C with winds around 23 km/h gusting to 42 km/h, forecast to reach a high of -2°C and a low of -6°C tonight. Conditions are firm and fast early on, gradually softening as temperatures warm through the day, with variable off-piste, firm in the shaded areas. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow's Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are all open, all 10 of 10 lifts running after Soho came back online this morning as wind eased; 9 of 10 terrain zones are open, with Arcadia Chutes on hold. Main Basin and Valley View open from 8:30am, with Captains and the T-Bar from 9am. The National Alpine Points races are on today at Upper Gold Rush, closed to the public until the race wraps up mid-morning. The access road is chain-free but chains must be carried given snow expected this afternoon, with an active road hazard advisory in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
