      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, truly into spring mode with firmer cold snow conditions first thing giving way to fantastic riding once the sun softens things up. Grooming has laid down plenty of freshly cut cord overnight; the natural base holds at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin, with no new snowfall in the past 24 hours. It's currently -2°C with light winds around 16 km/h gusting to 27 km/h, under clear blue skies, forecast to reach a high of -1°C and a low of -6°C tonight. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all open, all 3 of 3 lifts running; 7 of 9 terrain zones are open including Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Saddle Basin and Summit Slopes, with Matukituki Basin delayed and Motatapu Chutes closed. Backcountry and skinning access are both open; the access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Plant a Seed, a native tree-planting event supported by Mons Royale, runs from 1pm at the bottom of the access road. Four days remain in the season. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
